L245: 
L246: cite98†Image: side of a blue building with white windows jutting out into the water L247: ## A Durable Finish to Frame the View
L248: 
L249: Materials exposed to the sun and weather can lose brightness and color intensity over time, in addition to becoming brittle and breaking easily. To combat sun and weather exposure, door and window profiles are manufactured with polyvinyl chloride (PVC) because it offers:
L250: 
L251:   * Weather resistance
L252:   * Dependable thermal insulation
L253:   * Sound proofing
L254:   * A versatile range of architectural combinations
L255: PVC window and door profiles manufactured with Ti-Pure™ titanium dioxide (TiO₂) have excellent heat resistance and ~~ ~~weatherability, allowing them to withstand long-term exposure to the outdoors. Ti-Pure™ solutions enhance PVC profiles by:
L256:   * Increasing the lifetime by reducing brittleness and breakage
L257:   * Protecting against UV degradation, reflecting heat, and maintaining energy-efficiency
L258:   * Maintaining color integrity by resisting yellowing and discoloration
L259:   * Reducing oil canning or warping caused by extreme temperatures
